  "intentional_behavior_changes": [
    "Require exact signed-representable byte count from FAL instead of accepting every nonnegative result.",
    "TSL scratch32 and sector scratch104 are defined C arrays initializedff. Decode only after complete reads. TSL failure returns2 without changing caller record; sector failures mark sector byte0 invalid and return the error.",
    "Nested TSL failure propagates from sector traversal. Iterator checks each of its three TSL calls and exits through existing unlock path.",
    "Remove TSL/sector assembly bridges and read-adapter/FAL-read register constraints. Native private stack locations and stale bytes are no longer a read contract."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "Successful full-read record/status/diagnostic behavior matches stock in3549 comparisons. New error behavior is separately asserted in190 C-only cases, not stock-equivalent.",
    "Partition I/O and diagnostics are modeled in reader replay. FAL regression models lookup/device services.16 iterator error exits include4 normal-entry cases and12 controlled interior-callsite cases; the latter do not prove all normal search routes.",
    "Partial data reported falsely as a full count by an arbitrary provider is not independently detected; initialized scratch prevents uninitialized C data but does not validate provider truthfulness. The registered lower mapped-copy path was checked in the preceding completion review.",
    "No connection to physical flash, startup/layout or complete firmware boot is established. Buffer alias with private stack, arbitrary corruption, asynchronous callbacks and concurrency are outside these probes.",
    "Iterator remains symbolic assembly with three new error checks. Flash write constraints remain; no blanket assembly-free claim.852 units compile/compose with66 application and22 bootloader imports."
  ],
